---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, withBase } from '../data/site';
---

<Base>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="kicker">Studio</p>
    <h1>{site.tagline}</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Most AI tools help you be wrong, confidently. This studio is about systems, essays, and
      builds that hold the work to a standard — from a Principal Architect who still writes code
      and records what he learns.
    </p>
    <p>
      Essays land here first. Videos from{' '}
      <a href={site.youtube[0].href}>{site.youtube[0].name}</a>
      {' '}and{' '}
      <a href={site.youtube[1].href}>{site.youtube[1].name}</a>
      {' '}are curated, not dumped. GitHub repos become architecture notes, not a contribution graph.
    </p>
    <p>
      The next layer is an <a href={withBase('/atlas/')}>atlas</a>: ideas such as agents, evals,
      and null-safety, each pulling every essay, video, and build on that subject into one
      argument.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      The library is being moved in from{' '}
      <a href={site.articles}>articles</a>
      {' '}and{' '}
      <a href={site.ai}>ai</a>. Until then the shelves are honestly empty.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
